        "text": "{\"recorded_count\": 22, \"total_count\": 22, \"missing_ids\": [], \"complete\": true, \"results\": [{\"item_id\": \"FT-1\", \"verdict\": \"PASS\", \"issue\": null, \"actual\": null, \"evidence\": \"Create: \\\"QA Aeropress Go\\\" (Home Goods, $39.99, 4.3, image, https://example.com/qa-aeropress-go, tags qatag-travel/qatag-brewing, 2 specs, featured) appeared immediately in /products and on its detail page with all fields. Edit: changed every field incl. category Home->Fitness; card now reads \\\"Featured | Fitness | $129.5 | QA Trail Runner Pro | Lightweight trail shoe... | 4.9\\\" with the new image, and the detail page shows the new name, price, rating, description, edited review, specs (Drop=6mm, Lug Depth=4mm) and retailer link https://example.com/qa-trail-runner-pro. Tag and featured edits on seeded products (Philips Hue, Sony) also applied. Note: price renders as \\\"$129.5\\\" rather than \\\"$129.50\\\" (cosmetic).\"}, {\"item_id\": \"FT-2\", \"verdict\": \"FAIL\", \"issue\": \"Featured \\\"View all\\\" ignores the featured filter, so the complete featured set cannot be browsed\", \"actual\": \"Marking/unmarking does update the homepage: after unmarking Sony WH-1000XM5, the homepage featured strip changed from [sony, peloton, dyson] to [peloton, dyson, qa-aeropress-go]. However the strip is capped at 3 items, and the \\\"View all\\\" link (/products?featured=true) does not apply the featured filter - it renders \\\"10 products found\\\" listing every product including non-featured ones (samsung, macbook, bowflex, theragun, breville, philips). With 4 products featured, there is no view that shows the complete featured set.\", \"evidence\": null}, {\"item_id\": \"FT-3\", \"verdict\": \"PASS\", \"issue\": null, \"actual\": null, \"evidence\": \"\\\"SONY\\\" (uppercase) -> 1 product found, sony-wh-1000xm5 (name). \\\"FLAGSHIP\\\" -> 1 product found, samsung-galaxy-s24-ultra (tag-only match; word absent from visible card text). \\\"replace 15 sets\\\" -> 1 product found, bowflex-selecttech-552 (brief description). Counts matched displayed items in every case.\"}, {\"item_id\": \"FT-4\", \"verdict\": \"FAIL\", \"issue\": \"Tag-filter choice list is static and ignores tags added to products\", \"actual\": \"After saving tag \\\"qa-newtag\\\" (and renamed \\\"mood-lighting\\\") on the existing Philips Hue Starter Kit, the advanced tag-filter list still contained exactly the original 35 seeded tags. \\\"qa-newtag\\\" and \\\"mood-lighting\\\" are absent, so the new tag cannot be selected as a filter and cannot return the matching product. The list also still offers now-unused tags \\\"ambiance\\\" and \\\"automation\\\" (ambiance matches 0 products). Tags on a newly created product (qatag-travel, qatag-brewing) were likewise absent.\", \"evidence\": null}, {\"item_id\": \"FT-5\", \"verdict\": \"PASS\", \"issue\": null, \"actual\": null, \"evidence\": \"Created QA Aeropress Go with comma-separated new tags \\\"qatag-travel, qatag-brewing\\\". Both saved and render as separate tag chips on the detail page (product.tags.item.qatag-travel / .qatag-brewing). Keyword search \\\"QATAG-BREWING\\\" returns exactly 1 product found = qa-aeropress-go, so new tags participate in search.\"}, {\"item_id\": \"FT-6\", \"verdict\": \"PASS\", \"issue\": null, \"actual\": null, \"evidence\": \"Edited Philips Hue tags from [lighting, smart-home, ambiance, automation] to [lighting, smart-home, mood-lighting, qa-newtag] (added qa-newtag, renamed ambiance->mood-lighting, removed automation). Detail page shows exactly the new 4-tag set. Search \\\"qa-newtag\\\" -> 1 product = philips-hue-starter-kit; search \\\"ambiance\\\" (removed) -> 0 products found.\"}, {\"item_id\": \"FT-7\", \"verdict\": \"PASS\", \"issue\": null, \"actual\": null, \"evidence\": \"Admin form category is a single-select with exactly 3 options (Tech Gadgets / Home Goods / Fitness). Created \\\"QA Aeropress Go\\\" with Home Goods; admin row shows \\\"Home\\\", the